Subject: [PATCH 0022] one market view, one pair gate

PHASE 2.1 + 2.2. Applies on merged main (PR #9).

2.1 - ONE VIEW OF THE VENUE, OR A REFUSAL

main.tick makes THREE independent venue calls - perp mark, funding, spot mark -
and hands them to the engine as if they described the same instant. They do not.
Between the first and the third the venue moves, a rate prints, or one endpoint
serves a cached response while the others are live.

That matters more here than in a directional book because THE BASIS IS A
DIFFERENCE between two of those numbers. A perp mark from 09:00:00 against a
spot mark from 09:00:40 does not measure the basis; it measures the basis plus
forty seconds of drift - on a term 0018 measured at -$4,772 against $42,843 of
gross.

Worse: none of the three carried a timestamp. A VENUE THAT FREEZES AND SERVES
THE SAME TICK FOREVER LOOKS IDENTICAL TO A QUIET MARKET. The book would keep
trading on an hour-old price and never know.

 + market_snapshot.py   all four reads in one place, one observation time, the
                        venue's own clock where it publishes it.
                        assert_fresh() RAISES - it does not return a flag,
                        because a flag can be forgotten and this check must not
                        be passable.
                        A failed leg PROPAGATES rather than being omitted: a
                        snapshot missing a field it could not read is a partial
                        view wearing a complete one's clothes.
                        A venue that will not give its time disables the SKEW
                        check only; it is not a reason to refuse, and the
                        snapshot records that it was not checked.

2.2 - THE SIZE GATE THE PAIR DID NOT HAVE

RiskManager.gate_order guards every directional order in this tree: notional
cap, per-trade risk, leverage, daily loss, kill switch, quote sanity. THE CARRY
PAIR PASSES THROUGH NONE OF IT. That was a defensible choice - a hedged pair has
no stop distance, and daily loss limits assume directional P&L - and it was
never written down as one. The consequence is that max_notional_usd is currently
the ONLY size control on the book. At $100 harmless. At $1m it is the entire
risk framework.

